ect\n\nStar 0\n\nProject ID: 16\n\nMore actions\n\n## Project information\n\nCreated on\n\nJuly 06, 2022\n\nmaster\n\nCode\n\n  *     * Clone with SSH\n\n[Input]\n\n  *     * Clone with HTTPS\n\n[Input]\n\n  * Open in your IDE\n\n    * Visual Studio Code (SSH)\n    * Visual Studio Code (HTTPS)\n    * IntelliJ IDEA (SSH)\n    * IntelliJ IDEA (HTTPS)\n  * Download source code\n\n    * zip\n    * tar.gz\n\nDownload\n\n  * Download source code\n\n    * zip\n    * tar.gz\n    * tar.bz2\n    * tar\n\nCopy HTTPS clone URL\n\n  * Copy SSH clone URLgit@gitlab.shiawasedo.co.jp:external/paygent-connect.git\n  * Copy HTTPS clone URLhttps://gitlab.shiawasedo.co.jp/external/paygent-connect.git\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDocs, Paygent (https://api.paygent.tech/docs)\nciteturn3search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ## 2 Connect it to Claude Desktop ... Start a new chat, confirm Paygent is enabled for that conversation (look for a tools icon near the message box), and just ask naturally.\n\n# Connecting an AI agent\n\nGive your agent an API key, and it can request and fund a virtual card on your behalf using USDG or ETH on Robinhood Chain.\n\n## 1 Get your API key\n\nSign in to get one.\n\n## 2 Connect it to Claude Desktop\n\nClaude Desktop supports remote MCP servers on every plan, including free, with no special setup needed. Here is how to add Paygent.\n\n  1. Open Claude Desktop and go to Settings\n  2. Find Connectors (sometimes labeled MCP) and choose Add custom connector\n  3. Set the Name to `Paygent`\n  4. Set the Remote MCP server URL to your MCP URL with your API key appended as a query parameter, since some clients do not offer a separate header field:\n    \n    `https://mcp.paygent.tech/sse?api_key=pgt_live_your_api_key_here`\n\n  5. Leave the OAuth fields blank, then click Add\n  6. Start a new chat, confirm Paygent is enabled for that conversation (look for a tools icon near the message box), and just ask naturally. For example: \"Use Paygent to create a card for me.\"\n\nClaude will show you what it is about to do and ask for confirmation before calling any tool that funds or modifies something, so you stay in control at every step.\n## 7 Minimal Node.js client\n    \n    `import { Client } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/index.js\";\n    import { SSEClientTransport } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/sse.js\";\n    \n    const API_KEY = process.env.PAYGENT_API_KEY; // never hardcode this\n    \n    async function main() {\n      const transport = new SSEClientTransport(new URL(\"https://mcp.paygent.tech/sse\"), {\n        requestInit: { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${API_KEY}` } }\n      });\n      const client = new Client({ name: \"my-agent\", version: \"1.0.0\" }, { capabilities: {} });\n      await client.connect(transport);\n    \n      const created = await client.callTool({ name: \"create_card\", arguments: {} });\n      console.log(created.content[0].text);\n    \n      await client.close();\n    }\n    \n    main();`\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\nHow does Paygent control agent spending?\n\nEach card funds for exactly the amount deposited, with a hard cap set per account. There is no shared balance an agent could overdraw, and no card exceeds what was actually sent.\n\nWhat are Paygent virtual cards?\n\nReal, spendable card numbers issued automatically once a deposit confirms on chain. Each one is scoped to a single funding event, with its own number, expiry, and security code.\n\nHow secure are agent payments?\n\nYour API key is a bearer credential scoped to one account. Card details are only ever returned to a request authenticated with that key, and keys can be rotated instantly from your dashboard.\n\nCan I close a card and get funds back?\n\nYes. Calling `close_card` closes the card and refunds any remaining balance back to your wallet.\n\nDoes Paygent support MCP integration?\n\nYes, natively. Connect from Claude Desktop, Claude Code, or any MCP compatible client using the config shown above.\n\n## Notes\n\n  * Only one active card is allowed per account, so close the existing one before requesting another.\n  * Send any amount within the range returned by `create_card`, there is no need to specify an amount upfront.\n  * Sending more funds after a card is already active tops it up automatically, rather than creating a second card.\n  * Treat your API key as a bearer credential. Anyone with it can act on your account, so rotate it from your dashboard if it is ever exposed.\n\nQuestions or issues? Check your dashboard, or reach out to support.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFX Audit API & MCP — Developer Documentation — iPayX (https://www.ipayx.ai/developers)\nciteturn3search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Custom domain api.ipayx.ai coming soon.\n\nWORLD'S FIRST MCP-NATIVE FX AUDIT ENGINE\n\n# The Auditable Truth API & MCP for Modern Fintechs\n\nOne stable endpoint. A native MCP server. Audit-grade FX proof your sales team — or your AI agents — deliver in under 30 seconds.\n\nEvery FX audit you run today is part of the Vision FX foundation — the dataset that will power real-time anomaly detection for your stack.\n\nBuilt to become the FX signal layer behind future broker, treasury, and automation workflows.\n\nGet API KeyTry Sandbox\n\nREST API JSON responses Webhooks Production-ready\n\n### Powered by iPayX AI Engine\n\niPayX AI Engine reads bank statements, detects FX spreads, and returns structured JSON output. Every audit response includes a confidence score and spread benchmark.\n\nMCP Server — Model Context Protocol\n\n## The world's first MCP-native FX audit engine\n\nPlug iPayX directly into Claude Desktop, Cursor, ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot Studio, Perplexity, n8n. Your AI agents can audit an FX transfer, verify a rate, or generate a forensic report — without leaving their tool.\n\n`check_fx_rate`\n\nLive mid-market rate + spread analysis (public)\n\n`audit_transaction`\n\nScore 1-10, spread %, hidden fees (public, 10/IP/7d)\n\n`full_forensic_report`\n\nFull forensic report + Proof-Link (API key)\n\nMCP Server URL\n\n`https://mcp.ipayx.ai/mcp`\n\nCopy MCP URL\n\n[Button: Claude Desktop][Button: Cursor][Button: Copilot Studio]\n\nclaude_desktop_config.json Copy\n    \n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"ipayx-fx-audit\": {\n          \"url\": \"https://mcp.ipayx.ai/mcp\",\n          \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ipx_live_your_key\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\nQuickstart\n\n## FX Audit — Quickstart\n\nHere are three common ways to plug iPayX into your product.\n\n### FX broker / multi-currency platform\n\nSend each client FX conversion (CAD→USD, EUR→CAD, etc.) to the iPayX API and return a 0–10 FX score with estimated hidden costs.\n\n### Corporate treasury\n\nFeed your international payments (supplier invoices) into iPayX to compare bank rates vs mid-market and track margin impact.\n\n### Accounting firm / fractional CFO\n\nUse the API to audit your clients' FX conversions at year-end and generate a standardized report with score and potential savings.\n\nConnect your data\n\n## Three ways to send your transactions\n\nPick the source that fits your stack. All converge into the same FX audit engine.\n\nPlaid Available US & Canada\n\nRead-only bank connectivity. Automatic FX transaction extraction from North American accounts.\n\nCSV / PDF upload Available Global\n\nImport statements or receipts. Built-in OCR normalizes transactions automatically.\n\nREST API Available Global\n\nSend transactions directly via the API. Ideal for ERP, treasury, and platform integrations.\n\n### How it works\n\nData source\n\nNormalization\n\nFX audit engine\n\nStructured results\n\n## Get started in 3 steps\n\n1\n\n### Create your account\n\nAccess your dashboard and generate your production API key.\n\n2\n\n### Copy your API key\n\nAuthenticate using a Bearer token from your backend.\n\n3\n\n### Send your first request\n\nPost transaction data to the FX audit endpoint and receive a structured JSON response.\n\n## First request\n\nDirect API endpoint. Custom domain api.ipayx.ai coming soon.\n\n[Button: cURL][Button: Node.js][Button: Python]\n\nbash Copy\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhat is Paygent? | Paygent Documentation (https://docs.withpaygent.com/documentation/introduction/what-is-paygent)\nciteturn3search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; In short: Connect your app with the Paygent SDK, configure pricing in the dashboard, and let Paygent turn AI usage into accurate, itemized invoices — without manual reconciliation.\n\n# What is Paygent?\n\nPaygent is billing infrastructure for AI products.\n\nIf you sell AI agents, copilots, voice assistants, or API-backed automation, you face a problem traditional billing tools weren’t built for: cost and value are driven by usage, not seats alone. Token counts change every release. Voice calls mix LLM, STT, and telephony costs. Enterprise deals need setup fees, credit packs, and custom rates — all on one invoice.\n\nPaygent solves this end to end: track what your AI does, price it flexibly, and invoice automatically.\n\n## The problem Paygent solves\n\nWithout usage-aware billing  | With Paygent\n--- | ---\nSpreadsheets to reconcile API costs vs customer charges  | Real-time usage → revenue in one system\nOne flat subscription that loses money on heavy users  | Activity, outcome, credit, and hybrid pricing\nManual invoices every month  | Orders + automatic invoice generation\nNo margin visibility per agent or customer  | Cost and revenue dashboards per indicator\nWeeks to launch a new pricing experiment  | Plans, wallets, and fee stacks in the dashboard\n\n### Orders & invoices\n\nAn order is the subscription contract (customer, agents, plan, billing day, taxes). Invoices are generated automatically from active orders — you don’t create them manually.\n\n## Pricing models at a glance\n\nModel  | Type  | Docs\n--- | --- | ---\nSetup fee  | One-time  | Subscription Fees\nPlatform fee  | Recurring  | Subscription Fees\nSeat-based  | Recurring per user  | Subscription Fees\nActivity-based  | Per usage event  | Pricing Models\nOutcome-based  | Per result  | Pricing Models\nCredits / wallets  | Prepaid or postpaid  | Credit Currencies\nExternal costs  | Pass-through (telephony, etc.)  | External Costs\nCustom model rates  | Token/minute markups  | Custom Pricing\n\n## Who is Paygent for?\n\n  * AI SaaS founders launching usage-based or hybrid pricing\n  * Voice / video agent builders billing per minute, call, or outcome\n  * Enterprise AI teams needing setup fees, custom plans, and GST/VAT\n  * Platform teams reselling LLM access with credit packs and wallets\n\nWho Should Use Paygent? →\n\n* * *\n\n## Get started in 5 minutes\n\n  1. Create an account and get your API key\n  2. Quick Start — install SDK, create agent + customer, send first event\n  3. Create an order — activate billing\n  4. Optional: Plans, Credit Currencies, Taxes\n\nIn short: Connect your app with the Paygent SDK, configure pricing in the dashboard, and let Paygent turn AI usage into accurate, itemized invoices — without manual reconciliation.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nToolkit Radar — 100 apps, agent-researched for Composio buildability (https://toolkit-radar.vercel.app/)\nciteturn3search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Vendor ships its own MCP server (mcp-fx-audit, GitHub org iPAYX-Technologies) alongside a REST API, for Claude/Cursor/ChatGPT clients.\n| Ecommerce  | API key  | Self-serve · free  | REST medium · webhooks  | —  | —  | GREEN—  | ·\n\n#### Verdict\n\nFanBasis does have a real documented REST API (apidocs.fan) with self-serve API keys, but it's a small/niche vendor with thin public verification - buildable, lower confidence.\n\n#### Auth\n\nAPI key sent in the x-api-key header on every request; separate production (fanbasis.com) and sandbox (qa.dev-fan-basis.com) environments.\n\n#### Access\n\nSelf-serve signup (email/phone verified) then API key from dashboard; no approval step documented, but KYC for actually processing live payouts is unverified.\n\n#### API\n\nREST API (apidocs.fan): checkout sessions, subscriptions, customers, transactions, discount codes, refunds/disputes, webhooks.\n\n#### MCP\n\nNo MCP server, official or community, found for FanBasis.\n\n#### Gotchas\n\nName collides with unrelated 'Fanbase' apps; deeper API docs sit behind a dev-docs.fanbasis.com login so full endpoint list is unverified.\n\n#### Evidence\n\nauthapiaccessoverview\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStripe Integration | Paygent Documentation (https://docs.withpaygent.com/documentation/integrations/stripe-setup)\nciteturn3search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago;   * Step 1 — Connect Stripe in Paygent ... Connect your Stripe account to Paygent to collect invoice payments through Stripe Checkout.\nFor AI agents: a documentation index is available at the root level at /llms.txt. Append /llms.txt to any URL for a page-level index, or .md for the markdown version of any page.\n\nOn this page\n\n  * Prerequisites\n  * Setup overview\n  * Step 1 — Connect Stripe in Paygent\n  * Step 2 — Configure the Stripe webhook\n  * In the Stripe Dashboard\n  * Step 3 — Collect payments on invoices\n  * Option A — Generate a payment link manually\n  * Option B — Include a Stripe link in invoice emails\n  * How payment flow works\n  * Local development with Stripe CLI\n  * Manual payment recording\n  * Security\n  * Troubleshooting\n\nScroll to top\n\n# Stripe Integration\n\nConnect your Stripe account to Paygent to collect invoice payments through Stripe Checkout. Paygent generates secure payment links, sends them in invoice emails when configured, and automatically marks invoices as paid when Stripe confirms payment.\n\n##### \n\nWhat Paygent handles for you:\n\n  * Creates Stripe Checkout Sessions for unpaid invoices\n  * Maps Paygent customers to Stripe customers on first payment\n  * Verifies webhook signatures and records payments when checkout completes\n  * Stores API keys encrypted — only masked values are shown in the dashboard\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n  * A Stripe account with API access (test or live mode)\n  * At least one customer with an email address (required for automated invoice emails)\n  * An unpaid invoice with a total amount greater than zero\n\n## Setup overview\n\nStep  | Action  | Description\n--- | --- | ---\n1  | Connect Stripe in Paygent  | Add your Stripe secret key and webhook signing secret under Settings → Integrations.\n2  | Configure Stripe webhook  | Register Paygent’s webhook URL in the Stripe Dashboard and subscribe to `checkout.session.completed`.\n3  | Collect payments  | Generate a payment link from an invoice, or enable automatic Stripe links in order invoice emails.\n4  | Payment confirmed  | Stripe notifies Paygent via webhook; the invoice is marked paid automatically.\n\n* * *\n\n## Step 1 — Connect Stripe in Paygent\n\n  1. Open Settings → Integrations in the Paygent dashboard.\n  2. Toggle Stripe on (or click Edit if already connected).\n  3. Enter a connection name (for example, `Production Stripe`).\n  4. Paste your Stripe Secret Key — starts with `sk_test_` or `sk_live_`.\n  5. Paste your Webhook Signing Secret — starts with `whsec_` (you will get this in Step 2).\n  6. Click Save Connection.\n\n##### \n\nWhere to find your Stripe secret key: In the Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API keys, copy the Secret key. Use test keys while setting up; switch to live keys when you go to production.\n\n* * *\n\n## Step 2 — Configure the Stripe webhook\n\nPaygent needs Stripe to send a webhook when a customer completes checkout. The webhook URL is unique to your organization and shown in the Connect Stripe dialog after you save your connection.\n\nWebhook URL format\n    \n    https://api.withpaygent.com/api/webhooks/stripe/{your-organization-id}\n\n### In the Stripe Dashboard\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSign in, Paygent (https://api.paygent.tech/)\nciteturn3search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Paygent Docs ... Connect over MCP and your agent handles the rest.\nPaygent Docs\n\nPayments for AI agents\n\n# Sign in to get your API key.\n\nFund an address with USDG or ETH, a card is issued for exactly what arrives, and your agent spends it over MCP — in under a minute.\n\nContinue with Email Wallet X\n\nImage Paygent\n\nAgent issued\n\n••••  ••••  ••••  4242\n\nCardholder\n\nyour-agent\n\nNetwork\n\nRobinhood Chain\n\nRobinhood Chain USDG and ETH MCP compatible\n\n01\n\nFund your address\n\nSend USDG or ETH on Robinhood Chain — any amount you choose.\n\n02\n\nCard issued\n\nA card activates automatically for the exact amount received.\n\n03\n\nYour agent spends it\n\nConnect over MCP and your agent handles the rest.\n\nYour API key controls a real deposit address — treat it like a password. Read the docs →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nllms.txt (https://paygent.ai/llms)\nciteturn3search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; - [How It Works](https://paygent.ai/howitworks): Three-step process: Connect your payment data, receive AI-powered insights on fees and opportunities, take action with transparent processor recommendations. ... - [Request an Introduction](https://paygent.ai/request-an-introduction): Connect with vetted payment processors from our partner network who prioritize transparent pricing and long-term partnerships.\n\n<h1>Information for AI Crawlers</h1>\n<p>Paygent.ai provides structured information for AI language models and crawlers.</p>\n<h2>Machine-Readable Content</h2>\n<p>Our llms.txt file is available at: <a href=\"https://paygent.ai/hubfs/website-assets/llms.txt\">https://paygent.ai/hubfs/website-assets/llms.txt</a></p>\n<h3>What We Do</h3>\n<p>Paygent.ai helps small businesses understand payment processing costs through AI-powered analytics and education. We analyze statements, identify hidden fees, and connect businesses with transparent processors.</p>\n<h3>Key Resources</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/howitworks\">How Paygent.ai Works</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/aboutus\">About Our Mission</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/partner-network\">Partner Network</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n# Paygent.ai\n> AI-powered payment processing intelligence platform that helps small businesses understand their payment processing costs, reduce fees, and find the best-fit processor through transparent analytics and education.\n## About\nPaygent.ai brings clarity and fairness to payment processing, an industry long driven by complexity and confusion. Using AI to reveal patterns and hidden truths, we equip small businesses to act with confidence and thrive. We analyze fees, surface opportunities, and provide education—we never process or move funds directly.\n## Core Pages\n### Main Services\n- [How It Works](https://paygent.ai/howitworks): Three-step process: Connect your payment data, receive AI-powered insights on fees and opportunities, take action with transparent processor recommendations.\n- [What Is Paygent](https://paygent.ai/what-is-paygent): Free 24-hour payment processing audit that analyzes your fees, identifies hidden markups, and provides actionable recommendations without obligation.\n- [AI Positioning](https://paygent.ai/ai-positioning): How Paygent.ai uses artificial intelligence to analyze payment processing patterns, detect inefficiencies, and provide personalized cost-saving recommendations.\n- [Partner Network](https://paygent.ai/partner-network): Curated network of transparent payment processors who offer fair pricing and clear terms—high-intent introductions to processors aligned with transparency values.\n- [Reques